message: "If you cite this computational research thesis, please use the metadata below. No DOI is minted here; do not invent one."
type: thesis
title: "NSTG CaseCards as predicates for tip-ODE forcing admission without guideline-to-Θ leakage"
authors:
  - family-names: Ogbonna
    given-names: Kelechi Emeka
    email: kelechiogbonna300@gmail.com
    alias: cloudynirvana
abstract: >-
  Can NSTG CaseCards encode the Thesis #19 admission predicates so that
  guideline or knowledge text is refused as a coefficient write, while a
  protocol-constant known forcing with named provenance is still admitted?
  On this ledger they can. The legal card stores the checks as tokens and
  contains no digit. Two poisoned cards are refused by the loader. Twenty
  calls are issued. Nineteen return refused, including guideline prose aimed
  at a kinetic name, a numeral parsed from a dose-like sentence, a soft prior,
  and a score-copied amplitude. One call admits row_north as the provenance
  of u_phyto = 1. The SHA-256 of kinetic Θ is unchanged by that admission.
  The forcing digest changes. The admitted payload does not contain the
  guideline sentence. Research only. Not a medical device. No document DOI.
keywords:
  - NSTG CaseCard
  - admission predicate
  - known forcing
  - guideline leakage
  - kinetic parameter digest
  - tip ODE
  - provenance
  - research-only
